^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-27] note — server cost bounds are multi-client; Neovim CursorHold costs owned by neovim-spw-surfaces
 >>[2026-03-31 23:37] observe — the extension currently activates the LSP, annotation mirror, context strip, concepts tree, and workspace atlas immediately, even when the user only opens a `.spw` file and never touches the sidebar.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:38] observe — shipped startup still launches the server through `node --import tsx ...stdio-server.ts`, which keeps source-first convenience but taxes every activation path.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:39] observe — the client rebuilds the full annotation snapshot after each save, even though the server already updates saved/open documents and refreshes watched files incrementally.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:40] observe — cursor context is requested by both the status strip and the workspace atlas, so the same movement can produce multiple `spw/contextAtPosition` calls with different debounce timers.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:41] observe — semantic tokens still rescan full text via regex even though ServerIndex already stores parsed document state and line contexts.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:42] decide — the branch should optimize by ownership: startup costs, steady-state correctness costs, and visible-surface costs must be separated before any cache or debounce change lands.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:43] decide — the sidecar artifact will teach principles and tradeoffs explicitly so future VS Code work does not reintroduce client-side recomputation under new features.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:44] hygiene — base reference recorded at `main@d503198758b88f5894102609473997e02ca196ce`; `main...HEAD` shows no committed drift outside `.agents/plans/`.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:45] hygiene — unrelated local drift exists in `.agents/plans/v030-release-prep/wip.spw`; leave it untouched and out of scope for this plan.
 >>[2026-03-31 23:46] taste — a faster preview extension should feel quieter, not merely more deferred. Invisible surfaces should stop asking the LSP for truth they are not currently rendering.
 >>[2026-07-20 15:30] revise — measure the same paths from an identity-free mounted consumer and classify every performance claim by advertised, configured, invoked, observed, and tested evidence.
 >>[2026-07-20] revise — compiled LSP path already preferred when .js exists; remaining work is eager activation, incremental annotations, shared cursor bus, visibility gating, parse-backed tokens.
 >>[2026-07-20] decide — ladder rung 2 under vscode-lsp-roadmap; do not conflate with typescript-perf-audit-infra (tsc only).
 >>[2026-07-20] observe — hot sizes: display~1410 server-index~1160 atlas/concepts trees~725-750; extract before grow.
}

^["open"]{
